Subject: transcript markdown: the enhancement pass names when it changes marked's output

What: `markdownEnhances(html)` is exported next to the pass, and the pass's own
math and code-block gates are the ones it reads. A test holds, for prose, lists,
tables, math, fenced and indented code, that the pass changes marked's
synchronous output exactly when the predicate says so.
Why: the app paints a block from marked's synchronous output first and then runs
this pass. When the pass would return that output unchanged, the app keeps the
first-paint block instead of re-parsing it and replacing identical markup.

